From: alvesmaicon <alvesmaiconn@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] SendObject: remove the partial file when the host cancels

When the host cancels a SendObject (the user cancels a copy in the file
manager), the data loop stops, the file is closed and the operation
returns with no response, but the part already written stays on the
storage. The host no longer lists it, so it takes space the user can't
see or free from the host.

Remove the file and its entry, as DeleteObject does, and forget the
object handle. A cancelled SendPartialObject keeps its file: it edits a
file that was already there.

Upstream: not sent yet (viveris/uMTP-Responder, master has the same code)
---
--- a/src/mtp_operations/mtp_op_sendobject.c
+++ b/src/mtp_operations/mtp_op_sendobject.c
@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@
 #include "mtp_helpers.h"
 #include "mtp_constant.h"
 #include "mtp_operations.h"
+#include "mtp_ops_helpers.h"
 
 #include "usb_gadget_fct.h"
 
@@ -154,6 +155,19 @@
 						{
 							ctx->cancel_req = 0;
 
+							// The host gave the object up: don't leave the part already written behind,
+							// unseen by the host but taking space. A partial send edits a file that
+							// was already there, so that one stays.
+							if( mtp_packet_hdr->code != MTP_OPERATION_SEND_PARTIAL_OBJECT )
+							{
+								if( !set_storage_giduid( ctx, entry->storage_id ) )
+									delete_tree( ctx, ctx->SendObjInfoHandle );
+
+								restore_giduid( ctx );
+
+								ctx->SendObjInfoHandle = 0xFFFFFFFF;
+							}
+
 							pthread_mutex_unlock( &ctx->inotify_mutex );
 
 							return MTP_RESPONSE_NO_RESPONSE;
